 game and you know although I'm  extremely far from continuing to be  mentioned with them it's nice to be off  to this kind of starting to be in any  category with those guys so the best  thing I can do is just to stay focused  on the Open Championship coming in four  weeks time and and get prepared and get  ready to go to the home of golf a  special place to try and get that third  one mark brought up Arnold Palmer he was  among the first to take up endorsements  the question I have for you is do you  regret signing such a long-term deal  with Under Armour because you're worth a  lot more money right now no I don't  think I am I I don't regret it at all  the the terms of our ten-year extension  at least the impact that it was made on  me was that they expected me to win  major championships that's the trust  that they took and it just went along  the lines of the same trust they took  when they originally signed me and I  when I first turned professional so this  is nothing out of the ordinary or  unexpected based on the terms of the  deal and and I'm just pleased to be a  you know helping grow that company and  we're doing it together can you share  some of those terms if you do win the  slam what sort of bonus money is in  there for you no I can't it's in my  contract I'm not allowed to disclose the  information have Jordan I want to know  when you look at your players games  sorry  many of whom are still living oh don't  worry what do you see in the way in  their game and their lifestyle that you  try to incorporate into your own  well a lot of what I look up to  especially looking at the greatest  players in the game is I look at their  body language in the heat of the moment  I look at how they're handling  situations they get frustrated when they  when they don't pull off a shot that  they're you know that the the shot that  they want to hit but the way that the  way that you rebound the way that you  deal with adversity in the in the heat  of a major championship is is what  allowed them to win it that's what  affected me at the Masters in 2014 when  I wasn't able to close and that's what  I've improved on and it has established  a winning formula these last two majors  was when there was adversity whether it  was Thursday Friday or even the first  hole on Sunday it's how you bounce back  and realizing the length and the  duration that one major championship  around kind of takes on you and that's  what happened Jordan we're gonna have to  leave it there thank you so much for  joining us masters and US Open champion  jordan Spieth
 

